    {
      "id": "be-s9-forecasting-methods-c3",
      "heading": "Time series and causal models",
      "explanation_md": "Statistical forecasting has two kinds of model:\n\n- **Time series models** assume the **future will follow the same patterns as the past**.\n- **Causal models** explore **cause-and-effect relationships** and use **leading indicators** to predict the future. The slide's example: **housing starts** help predict **appliance sales**.",
      "example_ids": [
        "be-ex-housing-starts-appliances"
      ],
      "key_terms": [],
      "exam_line": "Time series: the past pattern continues. Causal: cause and effect with leading indicators (housing starts and appliance sales).",
      "clarification": null,
      "check_questions": [
        {
          "id": "be-s9-forecasting-methods-q-0be7ed66",
          "type": "mcq",
          "stem": "Using housing starts to predict appliance sales is an example of:",
          "options": [
            "A causal model",
            "A time series model",
            "The Delphi method"
          ],
          "answer": "A causal model",
