    {
      "id": "be-s9-forecasting-methods-c4",
      "heading": "What a time series is made of",
      "explanation_md": "**Data = historic pattern + random variation.**\n\nThe historic pattern can include:\n\n- **Level**: data moves sideways around a long-term average.\n- **Trend**: data rises or falls progressively.\n- **Seasonality**: a regularly repeating pattern, for example the same quarters peaking every year.\n- **Cycle**: data rises or falls over a longer stretch of time.",
      "example_ids": [],
      "key_terms": [],
      "exam_line": "Data = historic pattern (level, trend, seasonality, cycle) + random variation.",
      "clarification": null,
