    {
      "id": "be-s9-forecasting-methods-c5",
      "heading": "Methods, and how to choose one",
      "explanation_md": "The slides list four **methods of forecasting**: **ordinary least square**, **regression**, **moving average** and **exponential smoothing**.\n\nTo **select a model**, look at:\n\n- the **amount and type of data** you have\n- the **degree of accuracy** you need\n- the **length of the forecast horizon**\n- whether there are **patterns in the data**",
      "example_ids": [],
      "key_terms": [],
      "exam_line": "Choose a model by the data available, the accuracy required, the forecast horizon and the patterns in the data.",
      "clarification": null,
      "check_questions": [
